cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these engines in a project, video, paper or class, please credit them
  with a link back to https://github.com/ec175/spectrometry_public
type: software
title: "spectrometry.mp4 engines"
abstract: >-
  Python engines that turn real simulations into vertical video: 2-D fluid dynamics
  (lattice-Boltzmann and compressible Navier-Stokes), field lines of electric and
  magnetic fields, strange-attractor particle swarms, rigid-body shape physics with
  simulation-triggered audio, a simulated CRT oscilloscope with a film filter, and
  simulated FTIR, Raman, UV-Vis and NMR spectra for molecules.
authors:
  - given-names: Clancy
    family-names: Earl
    alias: spectrometry.mp4
repository-code: "https://github.com/ec175/spectrometry_public"
url: "https://ec175.github.io/spectrometry_public/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - scientific visualization
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - lattice Boltzmann
  - spectroscopy
  - generative art
  - creative coding
  - physics simulation
  - python
  - ffmpeg
  - manim
